{% comment %}
  KRAMSAKON — the header brand mark.

  Dawn's stock behaviour is to print the shop name as *text* when no logo image
  is set. That string comes from Settings → Store details, not from the theme's
  locale files, so Translate & Adapt cannot switch it per language — an English
  visitor would still be shown the Thai store name. The text fallback is
  therefore gone, and the wordmark ships with the theme instead.

  Two sources, in order:

  1. Theme settings → Logo, whenever the owner has uploaded one. This is an
     image_picker, so it gets the full responsive srcset through image_url and
     the owner can change it without touching code.
  2. assets/kram-logo.png — the KramSakon wordmark bundled with the theme, so
     the header is correct from the moment it is installed. Theme assets are
     static files rather than image objects, so image_url and its srcset are
     not available here; the file is stored at 600 × 256 (a little over 3× the
     default 180px display width) and scaled down by the browser.

  Accepts:
  - sizes:   {String} `sizes` attribute, uploaded-logo case only. Required.
  - classes: {String} extra classes for the <img>. Optional.

  Usage:
    {% render 'kram-header-logo', sizes: sizes, classes: 'motion-reduce' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- if settings.logo != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign logo_alt = settings.logo.alt | default: shop.name | escape
    assign logo_height = settings.logo_width | divided_by: settings.logo.aspect_ratio
    capture widths
      echo settings.logo_width
      echo ', '
      echo settings.logo_width | times: 1.5 | round
      echo ', '
      echo settings.logo_width | times: 2
    endcapture
  -%}
  {{
    settings.logo
    | image_url: width: 600
    | image_tag:
      class: classes,
      widths: widths,
      height: logo_height,
      width: settings.logo_width,
      alt: logo_alt,
      sizes: sizes,
      preload: true
  }}
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The alt text deliberately transcribes the words in the wordmark rather than
    echoing shop.name. It is the same in every language — a brand mark is not
    translatable content — and it stays correct even before the owner replaces
    the placeholder store name in Settings → Store details.

    600 × 256 is the stored size; height is derived from the owner's chosen
    width so the box is reserved before the image loads and nothing shifts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign kram_logo_height = settings.logo_width | times: 256 | divided_by: 600 -%}
  <img
    src="{{ 'kram-logo.png' | asset_url }}"
    alt="KramSakon"
    width="{{ settings.logo_width }}"
    height="{{ kram_logo_height }}"
    class="{{ classes }}"
    loading="eager"
    fetchpriority="high"
  >
{%- endif -%}
